<title>USA: Tropical storm Andres may flood parts of Guatemala.</title>
<headline>Tropical storm Andres may flood parts of Guatemala.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, MASS. 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Storm Andres, with 50 mph winds, is just off the coast of the Mexico/Guatemala Border and is moving east at 6 mph, forecaster Weather Services Corp said.</p>
<p>It would move inland and weaken across northern Guatemala and Belize. Heavy rain and flooding would be the main problem with this system, especially in western areas where mudslides were possible.</p>
<p>Wind damage was possible along the immediate coast over the next few hours.</p>
</text>
